{
  "id": "python_06_numbers_casting_en",
  "title": "Numbers and casting",
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "testId": "python_test_06_numbers_casting_en",
  "spans": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "WHY USE THIS?\n",
      "size": 20,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Numeric conversion prepares user input for calculations, but rounding and precision effects must be understood rather than hidden.\n\n",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "CORE EXPLANATION\n",
      "size": 20,
      "color": "#6A1B9A",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Conversion adapts external data to the type a program expects: ",
      "font": "NimbusSans",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "input()",
      "font": "NimbusSans",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " always returns str, and files or APIs may also provide text. ",
      "font": "NimbusSans",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "int('12')",
      "font": "NimbusSans",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " gives 12 and ",
      "font": "NimbusSans",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "float('0.5')",
      "font": "NimbusSans",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " gives 0.5; invalid text raises ValueError. ",
      "font": "NimbusSans",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "int(3.9)",
      "font": "NimbusSans",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " truncates toward zero, while ",
      "font": "NimbusSans",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "round(3.9)",
      "font": "NimbusSans",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " rounds. ",
      "font": "NimbusSans",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "bool('False')",
      "font": "NimbusSans",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " is True because every non-empty string is truthy. Validate before conversion; an unhandled conversion error can stop the program.\n\n",
      "font": "NimbusSans",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "EXAMPLE CODE\n",
      "size": 20,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "QUESTION: What will this code print? Predict first, then run it.\n",
      "size": 16,
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "whole = int('12')\nratio = float('0.5')\nprint(whole + 2, ratio)\nprint(int(3.9), round(3.9), bool('False'))",
      "showCopyButton": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "EXPECTED RESULT\n",
      "size": 20,
      "color": "#2E7D32",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "14 0.5\n3 4 True",
      "showCopyButton": false
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "LINE-BY-LINE WALKTHROUGH\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "whole = int('12')",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Binds the evaluated expression to a name; without the assignment, later lines cannot reuse that result.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "ratio = float('0.5')",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Binds the evaluated expression to a name; without the assignment, later lines cannot reuse that result.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "print(whole + 2, ratio)",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Runs an expression; print displays a value and calls may have side effects—without the line, that action does not occur.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "print(int(3.9), round(3.9), bool('False'))",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Runs an expression; print displays a value and calls may have side effects—without the line, that action does not occur.\n\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
